<article class="env-lemma" id="012D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/012D">Lemma <span data-tag="012D">12.23.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $(K, F, d)$ be a filtered differential object of $\mathcal{A}$. The spectral sequence $(E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 0}$ associated to $(K, F, d)$ has </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  d_1^ p : E_1^ p = H(\text{gr}^ pK) \longrightarrow H(\text{gr}^{p + 1}K) = E_1^{p + 1}  \]
</div>
  <p> equal to the boundary map in homology associated to the short exact sequence of differential objects </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \text{gr}^{p + 1}K \to F^ pK/F^{p + 2}K \to \text{gr}^ pK \to 0.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear from the formula for the differential $d_1^ p$ given just above Lemma <a href="/tag/012C" data-tag="012C">12.23.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>